# Line endings.
#
# The index has always been LF while a Windows working tree checks out CRLF, with nothing here to
# reconcile the two and core.autocrlf unset. Staging any file as-is therefore wrapped a whole-file
# rewrite around whatever actually changed, and `git diff` had to be read with --ignore-all-space
# to see the real work. Normalizing on commit settles it once, whatever a given checkout is
# configured to do.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Visual Studio rewrites these with CRLF the moment it touches them. Keeping them CRLF in the
# index is what stops every solution edit reading as a full-file diff.
*.sln              text eol=crlf
*.rc               text eol=crlf
*.props            text eol=crlf
*.props.template   text eol=crlf

# Byte-exact, and not text at all. The save-migration corpus in testing/fixtures is compared as
# bytes by the suite; left to the content heuristic one of these eventually guesses wrong.
*.sav   binary
*.lib   binary
*.dll   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary

# The tracked data dump (tools/dump/dump_data.py). Its decoded output is text,
# but the files it copies verbatim are not, and neither are the audio it writes.
*.wav   binary
*.lds   binary
*.exe   binary
*.ovl   binary
*.sf2   binary
*.awe   binary
*.pif   binary
*.box   binary
dump/raw/config/tyrian.cfg binary
